Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 06:40:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Shop products: filter the catalogue by category

The panel could list the catalogue and search it, but not ask the one question
that matters when a category looks empty: what is actually filed under it.

The filter is the SHOP's own facet, not a second opinion. It calls the same
`listCatalog` the storefront calls, with the same live `shop_categories` list, so
"6 products in Waxing products" here and "6 products" on the website are the same
statement. That is what makes a shelf the panel counts and the shop cannot show
visible in one click instead of from a customer's complaint.

- The select carries each category's product count.
- Any filter change returns to page 1.
- The header says how many products match and in which category, with Clear.
- An empty shelf says so plainly and names the category, instead of the
  "no catalog products yet" message that made it look like the list was broken.
